{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b736f4ac83559798","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9009\n3\tscore: 13\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: minor\n8\t  criterion: AI Implementability Scoring\n9\t  description: E001 ai_signals.human_process_gates is 0, but the rubric assigns +1\n10\t    when no human approval step remains and the epic rationale itself states PM approval\n11\t    is already recorded with only standard PR review left; value should be +1\n12\terror: null\n13\t---\n14\t## Review Summary\n15\t\n16\tScore: 13/14 — pass\n17\tRecommendation: accept\n18\t\n19\t## Criterion Details\n20\t\n21\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n22\tBoth HLR-1 and HLR-2 (both P2) map to RHAISTRAT-9009-E001, and the traceability matrix in the decomposition summary is present and complete (2/2 HLRs). Priority P2 matches the strategy's Minor priority. Priority-inheritance and priority-collapse checks do not apply: the strategy was triaged below-threshold (Step 0), which intentionally bundles all HLRs into a single epic, and both HLRs are at the same priority level anyway.\n23\t\n24\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n25\tTriage consistency check passes: `triage: below-threshold` with `epic_count: 1` is correct by design. Single-epic decomposition with no edges; the epic frontmatter `dependencies` is empty, matching the single-node DAG diagram. `critical_path_length: 1` is consistent with an S-sized strategy (heuristic range 1-2). No circular, invalid, or missing edges are possible in this structure. No conditional branch files exist, and none are required (no open questions).\n26\t\n27\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n28\tSingle epic covering a single component (Dashboard, verified against `.context/rhai-components.txt`) and a single team (RHOAI Dashboard). Scope is a string rename plus incidental documentation touch-ups — well under a sprint of work. The documentation updates are correctly folded into the same epic per the incidental-touch-up exception (no new content authored), so there is no work-product type mixing and no scope duplication.\n29\t\n30\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n31\tE001 is typed Implementation and produces a concrete artifact (the renamed label and updated doc topics). It is not misclassified — there is no uncertainty to resolve (strategy's Open Questions section is empty), so no Investigation epic is warranted. `gated_by` and `gate_failure_impact` are null, consistent with no gates. `implementation_type` is null, appropriate for a plain implementation.\n32\t\n33\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (1/2)\n34\tThe epic is Implementation-typed and correctly carries `ai_signals` (not `investigation_signals`); the ai-signals rationale file exists with a rationale per signal. Signal values check out against the rubric and the strategy: change_specificity 1 (exact string replacement specified), pattern_precedent 1, adapter_pattern 0 (N/A), existing_foundation 1 (pure extension of existing strings), open_questions 1 (none listed), external_dependency 1, repo_access 1, architecture_claims 0 (strategy makes no architecture claims; neutral is appropriate). One arguable value: `human_process_gates: 0` — the rubric defines +1 when no human approval step remains and -1 when one is required, and the epic's own rationale states PM approval is already recorded with only standard PR review remaining, which supports +1 rather than 0. This does not change the High classification and no arithmetic was checked (computed by the pipeline).\n35\t\n36\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n37\tE001 has five testable Given/When/Then acceptance criteria derived from both HLRs, including a negative criterion (no occurrence of the old label remains) and a guard criterion (no routing/API/CRD changes). Rule-mandated ACs: no replacement/rollback AC is required (this is a label change, not a component replacement), no konflux chain exists, and no docs-authoring epic exists (correctly folded per the triage exception). The epic body does not reference sibling epics by draft ID.\n38\t\n39\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n40\tAll strategy scope is covered: HLR-1 (navigation/headings label), HLR-2 (doc screenshot captions and references), and the out-of-scope boundaries (no CRD/K8s renames, no broader localization review) are explicitly carried into the epic's Scope and ACs. The strategy has no open questions, risks, dependencies, or Prerequisites & Process Gates section (no `Documentation Support: Yes`), so no docs-authoring epic is mandated and no strategy-level context was dropped. No conditional branches are needed.\n41\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-95139ba36e2a1835","agent_id":"ae9589aa9ac9b5fa6","session_id":"b717287d-85ac-464d-9f8c-187e04e74b79","uuid":"0590a8ab-c4db-46a4-bbfd-bccd76f5f04e","timestamp":"2026-10-21T20:35:24.965Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b736f4ac83559798","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9009 decomposition"}
